Apply only the test/registration portions first and run `DxUiTests --suite=MenuAccessibility --no-activate` to retain the expected failure at missing first child. Then apply the production portion and repeat in a fresh process. This draft was not built or run. `MenuResources` already emits matched plain-mode memory/handle samples; `MenuTextLayoutResources` has no menu or UIA tree and cannot attribute the new row objects.

The patches are split as `test-only.patch`, `resource-addendum.patch` (against the test-only checkout), and `production.patch`. Each was checked with `git apply --recount --check`; apply with `git apply --recount`. Run the resource addendum before the pre-fix semantic case to retain an old-pin resource receipt. It records 12/128-row plain menus, four open/close cycles each, matching source text, anchor, theme, 300-DIP maximum height, 456-DIP minimum width, physical geometry, bounded UIA navigation, and process/heap observations. The resource numbers are descriptive observations, with no asserted cost threshold or attribution of whole-process memory to individual rows.

Contract follow-up: `Specs/UI/UI_InputAndAccessibility.md` lines 25–34 currently say “Described native menus”; after qualification, clarify that full UIA roles, names, bounds, invocation, and disconnect apply to ordinary one-line menus as well. Review `Specs/UI/UI_ControlsAndLayout.md` 78–82 for the same semantic requirement. No gallery visual change is expected because the patch leaves layout and drawing untouched, but the repository's docs/gallery gate still applies.
